{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What services does ELM Construction provide?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We work across five core areas: kitchen remodeling, bathroom remodeling, basement renovations, additions, and outdoor living. We also take on whole-home renovations and restoration work, including fire restoration. Design is handled in-house, so a single team carries your project from concept through construction."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does a kitchen remodel with ELM typically include?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Kitchen projects are built around how you actually use the room. That usually means premium stone or quartz surfaces, professional-grade appliances integrated cleanly into the design, custom storage that uses every inch, layered lighting that works from morning to evening, and thoughtfully planned work zones that improve flow. Every element is selected with you rather than pulled from a package."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What can be included in a bathroom renovation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Bathroom renovations range from a guest bath refresh to a full primary suite transformation. Common elements include heated floors, freestanding soaking tubs, custom shower experiences with artisan tile work, premium fixtures in timeless finishes, and intelligent storage that keeps sight lines clean and the space free of clutter."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What can I do with an unfinished or underused basement?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A basement is usually the least expensive square footage in a house to make livable. We have converted lower levels into entertainment zones with proper acoustics, climate-controlled wine cellars, private fitness studios, executive home offices, and fully appointed guest suites. The right answer depends on your ceiling height, existing systems, and how you want to live in the space."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you build home additions?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. We design and build additions as well as whole-home renovations, and we handle the structural, permitting, and design coordination that additions require. Whether it makes more sense to build up with a second story or out with a ground-level addition depends on your lot, your existing structure, local zoning and setbacks, and your budget."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What kinds of outdoor living spaces do you build?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We build outdoor spaces designed to be used, not just looked at: professional-grade outdoor kitchens, all-season rooms with retractable screens, contemporary decks in premium hardwoods, and integrated lighting that keeps the space usable after dark. The goal is to extend your living area past the exterior walls."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you handle restoration work such as fire damage?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Restoration work, including fire restoration, is part of what we do alongside remodeling and additions. Because we are a design-build firm, we can rebuild what was lost and improve the layout at the same time rather than simply restoring the space to what it was."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What do projects like these typically start at?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "We publish starting figures so nobody wastes time. Per our Budgeting Guide, typical starting prices are: Complete kitchen remodel: $100,000; Kitchen \"facelift\": $70,000; Primary bathroom remodel: $70,000; Hall or guest bath remodel: $39,000; Basement remodel or finishing: $100,000; Porch remodel or addition: $95,000. Final cost depends on scope, material selections, and any structural changes. At the end of project development you receive a contract with a detailed scope of work and a guaranteed fixed price - a lump sum, with allowances clearly called out for items where your selections may vary."
      }
    }
  ]
}

